{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The priests, the Levites, shall have no portion.</b> Just as he mentioned the laws of the king—who is the judge—he also mentioned the law of the priests, who are the teachers of the Torah. And after stating that they have no inheritance, they shall receive from the one who slaughters: the arm, the cheeks, and the stomach. The arm is from the body, the cheeks—that the tongue is between them—are from the head, and the stomach from the entrails. By way of derash: since the priest is the one who slaughters the shelamim, the arm is the wages of his arm in the slaughter, the cheeks are the wages of the blessing, and the stomach is the wages of the inspection. By way of peshat: these are the choicest parts of the meat. He also mentioned the words of Levi, for they too teach Torah in the gates; the proof is Chronicles."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:53.103832461Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}